sections.body:
All three go in `internal/engine/specdraft_test.go` and use `specHarness` and `h.runner.requests()`.
- TestSpecDraftDenialResumeAsksForTheSectionBlocks: the first run returns `Result{Exit: ExitOK, Session: "sess", Report: draftReport, Denials: [one denied command]}`. The second request has `Resume == "sess"`. Its `Brief` must:
  - name the denied command;
  - contain `## Section NAME` and each of Why, Files, Failing tests, Implement and Check;
  - contain `## Owner needed`;
  - not contain `## Slice`, `Ready` or `Question:` as the form the report takes.

  This fails now because the draft reuses `specDenialNudge`.
- TestSpecDraftShapeResumeAsksForEverySection: the first reply is malformed (`strings.ReplaceAll(draftReport, "## Section ", "## ")`). The second request's `Brief` must contain the shape error. It must also say that every one of the five sections goes in again, with the new text or `unchanged`, even where the earlier report was right, and that the owner questions go in the same reply. This fails now because the shape nudge says "Write the whole report again" but never says the sections must be repeated.
- TestSpecDraftDenialResumeThatSendsTheFullReportPasses: the first reply carries a denial. The resumed reply is the full `draftReport`. `RunSpecDraft` returns the parsed draft with five sections, and no `spec-draft-failed-*.md` file is left.
